  "description": "Pigeon proof of work. preimage = lp(domain) || challenge fields || lp(nonce), where lp(x) = uint32be(byte length) || ASCII bytes. Identity admission fields: lp(identityId) || uint32be(network count) || lp(networkId) for each network sorted by bytes. Mailbox creation fields: lp(mailboxId) || lp(postTokenHash) || lp(readTokenHash). The proof is valid when SHA-256(preimage) starts with at least difficultyBits zero bits. Fields are 1 to 256 visible ASCII characters (0x21-0x7e); identity admission takes 1 to 64 distinct networks. Nonces are canonical decimal strings of 1 to 16 digits. difficultyBits is an integer from 1 to 32. Minted nonces are the first valid counter from 0.",
